# Staging Firebase config — chalkie-app-staging
#
# To run or build the app against staging instead of production:
#   1. Copy this file to mobile/.env.local (gitignored, already auto-loaded
#      by Expo — see mobile/.gitignore's ".env*.local" entry).
#   2. Fill in the two required values below from:
#      Firebase Console → chalkie-app-staging project → Project settings
#      → General → Your apps → "Chalkie Staging" (the registered web app)
#      → SDK setup and configuration → Config.
#   3. Run `npx expo start --web` or `npx expo export -p web` as normal —
#      no other command-line flags needed.
#
# None of these values are secret in the way an API key for most services
# is — Firebase's web config is meant to be embedded in client-side code
# and is protected by Firestore/Auth security rules, not by being hidden.
# Still kept out of git here for cleanliness and so staging/production
# can't drift into the wrong build by accident — see firebase.ts's isStaging
# guard for the actual safety property (a staging build refuses to start if
# either required value below is missing, rather than silently falling back
# to anything else).

EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_ENV=staging

# Required — Firebase-generated per project/app, cannot be derived or
# guessed. Copy exactly from the Firebase Console.
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STAGING_API_KEY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STAGING_APP_ID=

# Optional — default below is derived from the project ID
# (chalkie-app-staging, as given) using Firebase's standard naming
# convention. Uncomment and override only if your Firebase Console shows
# a different exact value (e.g. the project ID ended up auto-suffixed
# because "chalkie-app-staging" was taken).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STAGING_PROJECT_ID=chalkie-app-staging
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STAGING_AUTH_DOMAIN=chalkie-app-staging.firebaseapp.com

# Optional — this app does not use Firebase Storage or Cloud Messaging
# anywhere, so neither of these has any effect on app behavior. Leave unset
# unless you have a specific reason to set them.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STAGING_STORAGE_BUCKET=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STAGING_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
